#: ../../source/components_basic/24-component_rgb.rst:94
msgid "Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/24-component_rgb.rst:96
msgid "The first segment of the code declares and initializes the pins to which each color channel of the RGB LED module is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/24-component_rgb.rst:104
msgid "The ``setup()`` function initializes these pins as OUTPUT. This means we are sending signals OUT from these pins to the RGB LED module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/24-component_rgb.rst:114
msgid "In the ``loop()`` function, the ``setColor()`` function is called with different parameters to display different colors. The ``delay()`` function is used after setting each color to pause for 1000 milliseconds (or 1 second) before moving on to the next color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/24-component_rgb.rst:126
msgid "The ``setColor()`` function uses the ``analogWrite()`` function to adjust the brightness of each color channel on the RGB LED module. The ``analogWrite()`` function employs Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) to simulate varying voltage outputs. By controlling the PWM duty cycle (the percentage of time a signal is HIGH within a fixed period), the brightness of each color channel can be controlled, allowing the mixing of various colors."
msgstr ""

